WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.467
-That's exactly what I'm talking about.

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:04.601
Chris Evans, welcome. -How are you, buddy?

00:00:04.601 --> 00:00:06.868
[ Cheers and applause ] -That's got to feel good.

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:09.801
-Yeah. Yeah, every time. -Welcome back to the show.

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:12.467
-Thanks, man. -It is always great to see you.

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:14.734
You've been such a good friend to the show.

00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:16.334
Since I've last seen you, though,

00:00:16.334 --> 00:00:19.300
some major thing happened. I don't know if you saw this.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.501
You were named Sexiest Man Alive.

00:00:21.501 --> 00:00:22.934
-That's right.

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:24.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:27.601
♪♪

00:00:27.601 --> 00:00:29.067
That's right, that's right. That's right.

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:30.200
-You all right? You know what I'm saying?

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:33.133
-That's right, that's right. -Yeah.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.834
You put, "Thanks, People.

00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:37.901
I think we can all agree that it's damn near impossible

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:40.534
to follow in Paul Rudd's footsteps in any capacity,

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:42.501
but I'll do my best." -Which is true.

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:44.367
I mean, pretty much in any capacity,

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:45.767
it's tough to follow him, isn't it?

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:48.567
-Yeah. Did you hear anything from Paul Rudd since, uh...

00:00:48.567 --> 00:00:51.100
-Yeah, I'm -- Actually, I'm in a fantasy football league

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.534
with Paul and a few other actor buddies.

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:57.033
So they haze you, and it almost feels like

00:00:57.033 --> 00:01:01.667
that's all that title does is give you a hard time, you know?

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:05.400
Yeah, nobody on the street's like, "Hey. You know what?

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.834
You did it." [ Laughter ]

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.400
-"Congratulations." Yeah. No, everyone's like...

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.334
-No, they're just -- They're just busting your balls.

00:01:11.334 --> 00:01:13.467
-Yeah, you're like -- Well, that's good.

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:15.033
How did you do on the fantasy football team?

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.334
-Well, I didn't do well this year,

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:18.567
but I've won a few times, so I have bragging rights.

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:21.467
-All right. Yeah. Yeah. [ Cheering ]

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:22.968
I wanted to ask you this question

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:25.234
because I found this very interesting.

00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:26.701
I think that you might --

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:29.467
I have to thank you and give you credit for my first ever --

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:32.234
-I heard this. You -- go, go. This is amazing.

00:01:32.234 --> 00:01:34.534
Your producer told me this. -My acting debut,

00:01:34.534 --> 00:01:36.734
my television debut... -Was...

00:01:36.734 --> 00:01:38.300
-...was "Spin City."

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:42.701
-Which is where I interned in the casting office.

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:44.868
Around the same time? Did I --

00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:46.701
-I think you -- -Did I give you your first job?

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:48.167
-Wow! [ Laughter ]

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:51.834
I mean, this is -- I feel like I owe my whole career to you.

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:53.234
-What year was it? I mean, it was '98.

00:01:53.234 --> 00:01:55.634
-'98. -'98?!

00:01:55.634 --> 00:01:57.434
-I played -- I played -- -You're welcome.

00:01:57.434 --> 00:01:59.901
-Wow! [ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:59.901 --> 00:02:01.601
Wait. So... -Yeah.

00:02:01.601 --> 00:02:03.834
-I mean, for real. I remember I was nervous.

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:05.133
I went in. I read for this role

00:02:05.133 --> 00:02:08.067
as a photographer number one or something.

00:02:08.067 --> 00:02:10.167
-Yeah. -And I -- And I walked in,

00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:13.033
I -- and I didn't do anything that special.

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:14.801
So I'm like, "I'm not gonna get this."

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.133
But -- -But you got it.

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:17.834
-You did it. [ Laughter ]

00:02:17.834 --> 00:02:19.701
-What can I say? -But how --

00:02:19.701 --> 00:02:20.868
I don't understand.

00:02:20.868 --> 00:02:22.868
How old were you? What were you doing?

00:02:22.868 --> 00:02:24.734
-It was the summer of my junior

00:02:24.734 --> 00:02:26.000
going into senior year.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.968
I knew I wanted to act, so I moved to the city.

00:02:27.968 --> 00:02:30.501
I got a job interning at a casting office

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:32.267
just to meet agents, you know?

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:34.334
And it was -- -Did that work?

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:35.434
-It did, actually.

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:37.200
It's a humbling experience, though.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.834
I mean, you come into your job on a Monday

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:42.067
after there's -- an audition goes out.

00:02:42.067 --> 00:02:43.701
What was -- What was the part you had?

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:45.467
-Photographer number one. -Photographer number one, yeah.

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:47.567
So you show up at your desk -- -Hold your applause.

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:48.701
[ Laughter ] -You got -- you got --

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.868
-You remember it. -A stack of envelopes

00:02:50.868 --> 00:02:52.934
from all these agents in town. -Headshots and...

00:02:52.934 --> 00:02:54.601
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. And your boss comes in --

00:02:54.601 --> 00:02:56.434
And I don't want to get anybody in trouble,

00:02:56.434 --> 00:02:58.167
specifically my old boss, but she --

00:02:58.167 --> 00:02:59.968
she would pluck out two or three envelopes,

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:02.534
and I threw the rest in the trash.

00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:04.300
She just chucked them. And you were just like,

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:07.000
"Wow. This industry is brutal." -Oh, really?

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.334
-It's that brutal, tight?

00:03:08.334 --> 00:03:10.367
Because you go, like -- You're just trying to get hired.

00:03:10.367 --> 00:03:12.033
I mean, I didn't have an agent. I didn't --

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:13.400
I don't know how I got in there. -Yeah.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.033
Well, you certainly can't get upset at your agent.

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:17.067
That's what it told me. Your agent can be trying,

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:19.601
but, you know, sometimes they end up in the trash.

00:03:19.601 --> 00:03:21.200
-Yeah, it's just a pile of stuff.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.801
And then you just saw my headshot,

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:23.834
and you were like... -And I was like,

00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:25.567
"This guy's got something."

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:26.801
-You're like, "This guy..."

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:28.033
-I thought it was gonna be your headshot!

00:03:28.033 --> 00:03:31.634
-No, no, no! It was like, "This guy should be..."

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:35.234
But do you remember casting any other famous talk-show host?

00:03:35.234 --> 00:03:37.467
-No, I -- I -- [ Laughter ]

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:40.167
I just sat in the front room, setting up auditions.

00:03:40.167 --> 00:03:41.801
I remember some actors would come in.

00:03:41.801 --> 00:03:45.033
I remember seeing Jesse -- young Jesse Eisenberg.

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:46.767
-Yeah? -Young Jim Gaffigan

00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:48.100
would come in there a lot. -That's wild.

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:49.501
-But again, these are -- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:49.501 --> 00:03:51.300
I mean, this is back in like '98.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:54.567
-Yeah. I want to talk about your movie, "Ghosted."

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:57.400
It's on Apple TV+. It's a romantic comedy.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:59.167
You, Ana de Armas. It is like --

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:00.501
-Whoo! -Yeah, exactly.

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:02.400
And you two together. Yeah.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:07.133
So, the idea is that you guys meet-cute, you go on a date,

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:09.234
and then you think she may have ghosted you?

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:12.133
-Yep. -And then you -- you find her.

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:14.634
She -- She -- -Find her, track her down.

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:16.767
Kind of stalker my way... [ Laughter ]

00:04:16.767 --> 00:04:18.434
You know, you have this amazing date.

00:04:18.434 --> 00:04:20.400
You have this wonderful experience with someone.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.300
You go home, you tell your family, your friends,

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:23.400
and then you don't hear from her.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.734
She -- She ghosted me.

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:27.067
[ Audience groans, "Oohs" ]

00:04:27.067 --> 00:04:29.033
-Yeah. Listen to this reaction. [ Laughter ]

00:04:29.033 --> 00:04:30.434
Can you believe this? Yeah, I know.

00:04:30.434 --> 00:04:34.000
I was in tears. I go, "What?!"

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.167
Not my Chris. [ Laughter ]

00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:38.801
But you -- She has actually --

00:04:38.801 --> 00:04:40.234
It was like an Apple Tag.

00:04:40.234 --> 00:04:42.767
You have, like, a tracker that she takes,

00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:45.133
like your jacket or something. -Yeah.

00:04:45.133 --> 00:04:46.667
-Your inhaler? -I think it's my inhaler.

00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:48.701
It's a lot less cool than my jacket.

00:04:48.701 --> 00:04:49.801
-Sorry. -It's my inhaler.

00:04:49.801 --> 00:04:51.033
-She has your inhaler, and you go,

00:04:51.033 --> 00:04:52.234
"I know where she is." -"I know where she is."

00:04:52.234 --> 00:04:53.801
And my family's like, "You should go."

00:04:53.801 --> 00:04:55.767
You think -- You know -- he's, you know --

00:04:55.767 --> 00:04:57.701
he thinks it's a big grand, romantic gesture,

00:04:57.701 --> 00:04:59.400
and he ends up getting -- 'Cause she's a spy,

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.868
and he ends up getting caught up in this world of espionage.

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.968
-It's super fun. And you go, "Oh, my gosh.

00:05:03.968 --> 00:05:05.767
"Two..." plug your ears --

00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:08.667
"...really good-looking people in this thing."

00:05:08.667 --> 00:05:11.534
And I just loved the whole idea. Have you ever been ghosted?

00:05:11.534 --> 00:05:12.801
Do you know what that feels like, Chris?

00:05:12.801 --> 00:05:14.901
-You know, that's like the number-one question

00:05:14.901 --> 00:05:16.667
I'm getting asked on this press tour. I mean --

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:18.067
-You can say. No one's listening.

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:19.734
-Well, you know -- [ Laughter ]

00:05:19.734 --> 00:05:21.834
I don't know. I've probably blocked it out

00:05:21.834 --> 00:05:24.734
if it's happened. Have you?

00:05:24.734 --> 00:05:26.400
-Be honest. [ Laughter ]

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:28.133
-I'm too old to kind of --

00:05:28.133 --> 00:05:29.667
Well, see, I kind of feel the same way.

00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:31.000
-Does letters count? I mean --

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:32.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:34.801
Texting didn't exist when I was dating, you know?

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:36.934
-Your pen pal just fell off. -Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:36.934 --> 00:05:38.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:39.901
-Ran out of ink, you know? You know?

00:05:39.901 --> 00:05:41.834
Yeah. I didn't get a pen -- Exactly.

00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:44.033
But, I mean, I'm sure I was.

00:05:44.033 --> 00:05:46.234
I mean, there's definitely moments where I go,

00:05:46.234 --> 00:05:49.067
"Oh, they they're not into me." -Well, see, what

00:05:49.067 --> 00:05:50.968
I say is I'd almost rather be ghosted

00:05:50.968 --> 00:05:52.534
because you can tell yourself a story.

00:05:52.534 --> 00:05:54.501
Like, maybe they, you know, lost their phone.

00:05:54.501 --> 00:05:56.100
If you've had the worst,

00:05:56.100 --> 00:06:00.200
which is just kind of a gradual, less and less and less text,

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:03.100
then there's really no confusing what's going on.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:05.534
-Yeah, it's heartbreaking.

00:06:05.534 --> 00:06:08.200
But I will say there's some other cameos

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:09.934
that I don't know if I'm allowed to talk about.

00:06:09.934 --> 00:06:11.133
-There are some cameos,

00:06:11.133 --> 00:06:12.701
which you're not allowed to talk about,

00:06:12.701 --> 00:06:15.067
which I just learned right before we came out.

00:06:15.067 --> 00:06:16.601
So... [ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:16.601 --> 00:06:17.968
Good thing I didn't say anything.

00:06:17.968 --> 00:06:19.100
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.133
But they're great cameos.

00:06:20.133 --> 00:06:22.067
-But they're really great cameos.

00:06:22.067 --> 00:06:24.367
-Yeah, there's some friendly faces.

00:06:24.367 --> 00:06:25.567
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:25.567 --> 00:06:27.567
Some faces that you've seen before.

00:06:27.567 --> 00:06:29.367
-Yeah. Yeah. -Can I --

00:06:29.367 --> 00:06:31.234
Legally, I can say that. -I hate asking people

00:06:31.234 --> 00:06:34.033
for cameos. It's such an awful thing to do.

00:06:34.033 --> 00:06:35.267
-Oh, I wouldn't know what it's like.

00:06:35.267 --> 00:06:36.567
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.567 --> 00:06:39.534
I'm very available. [ Laughter ]

00:06:39.534 --> 00:06:41.667
It's -- The people that make the cameos

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:44.601
are super good and super funny. -They're fantastic.

00:06:44.601 --> 00:06:46.467
-And they're people that you love and you go --

00:06:46.467 --> 00:06:48.133
-And they they showed up. They showed up for me.

00:06:48.133 --> 00:06:50.634
We asked. -So now show up for Chris Evans.

00:06:50.634 --> 00:06:51.901
Here we go. I want to show a clip.

00:06:51.901 --> 00:06:54.033
Here's Chris Evans and Ana de Armas in "Ghosted."

00:06:54.033 --> 00:06:55.267
Take a look at this.

00:06:55.267 --> 00:06:58.267
[ Dramatic music plays ]

00:06:58.267 --> 00:07:08.334
♪♪

00:07:08.334 --> 00:07:13.567
♪♪

00:07:13.567 --> 00:07:15.367
[ Electricity crackles, man grunts ]

00:07:15.367 --> 00:07:16.367
Unh!

00:07:16.367 --> 00:07:17.767
-[Bleep]

00:07:17.767 --> 00:07:23.734
♪♪

00:07:23.734 --> 00:07:26.033
-Kimberly, you took a picture of me while I was sleeping.

00:07:26.033 --> 00:07:27.634
-Not of you! Of us!

00:07:27.634 --> 00:07:29.567
-I knew you were a creep!

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:34.400
-I'm not a creep!

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.701
-You know who says that a lot?

00:07:35.701 --> 00:07:37.300
Creeps!

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:39.634
-Oh! Come on! [ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:39.634 --> 00:07:42.667
Chris Evans! "Ghosted" premieres globally

00:07:42.667 --> 00:07:45.234
on Apple TV+ this Friday.

00:07:45.234 --> 00:07:47.234
Chris and I are doing "The Whisper Challenge"

00:07:47.234 --> 00:07:48.300
when we come back.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:49.634
Stick around, everybody. Come back.

